  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/... A cold front on Friday will \ndrop temperatures down to near normal. Ahead of this cold front, \nTropical Storm Iselle will weaken, with its remnant moisture \ntransported over our area in southwesterly flow aloft. As the long \nrange ensemble guidance sees it, PWAT values across southwest \nIdaho will increase to around the 95th percentile of climatology\n(highest near the Magic Valley and eastward). The timing of the\ncold front and moisture advection right now looks favorable for\nthe development of showers and thunderstorms come Friday \nafternoon, mainly in SW Idaho and the southeastern portions of \nthe Great Sandy Desert. With high PWATs, heavy rain will be a \nhazard with storms that develop and the flash flood risk will \nneed to be monitored. \n\nThe cold front and associated upper trough will be quick to push the \nmoisture off to the east come Saturday. The weekend will feature \ngenerally dry conditions with temperatures at or below normal. Come \nMonday/Tuesday, another trough digging down the coast of British \nColumbia and grazing our area will bring a slight chance of \nprecipitation across higher terrain of southwest Idaho. This fall-\nlike transition pattern looks to continue beyond the long-term \nperiod, with the extended outlooks leaning towards above normal \nprecipitation and below normal temperatures.&&",
